# 🎬 Creative Formulas: Video Storytelling Architecture

Where the **Creative Matrix Framework** maps performance coverage and identifies gaps, this document covers **narrative concepting**. 

Instead of treating video ads as static scripts or templating against rigid timeline-based rules (e.g., 0–3s, 3–7s rules), this framework treats video as an interchangeable 3-part storytelling engine. 

The actualities of each building block vary based on intended campaign outcome, but the overarching objective remains constant: earn attention, sustain engagement, and compel action.

---

## 🏗️ Building A Modular Concepting Engine

┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        3-PART CONCEPTING ENGINE                         │
├───────────────────┬───────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────┤
│ Core Phase        │ Viewer Psychology │ Strategic Function              │
├───────────────────┼───────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤
│ 1. The Hook       │ "Stop the Scroll" │ Earn immediate attention        │
│ 2. The Body       │ "Keep Watching"   │ Deliver the narrative & style   │
│ 3. The Resolution │ "Make Them Stay"  │ Propose solution & prompt action│
└───────────────────┴───────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────┘---

### Part 1: Hook (Stop the Scroll)

* **Objective:** Earn the viewer's attention
* **Strategic Driver:** This should be grounded in what the persona organically consumes and/or the specific tension, problem, or desire they have top of mind.
* **Concepting Levers:** These will be further dissected in video-creative-engineering, but unlocking niche hooks, tailored to your industry/product/persona will help you stand out.
  
---

### Part 2: Body (Keep 'Em Watching)

* **Objective:** Give the viewer a reason to stay past the hook by pairing valuable information with a distinct delivery style.
* **Strategic Driver:** Concept a compelling vehicle for communicating to your audience. There must have a clear purpose beyond selling a product.
* **Concepting Levers & Delivery Styles:** These will be further dissected in video-creative-engineering, but impactful levers will create value for viewers.

---

### Part 3: Resolution & Invitation To Action (Make Them Stay & Act)

* **Objective:** Connect the narrative back to an outcome that's mutually beneficial for the business and the viewers. Give them a clear reason to look up the brand/product/solution.
* **Strategic Driver:** Directly proposes a solution to the problem introduced in the Hook and elaborated through the Body. The most meaningful as it shifts the viewer from passive consumption to active intent.
* **Concepting Levers:** These will be further dissected in video-creative-engineering, and their efficacy is reliant on how well they suit parts one and two. Ergo, you should aim for a unique delivery that transforms the simplified thoughtstarters or traditional CTAs.

---

## 🧪 Modular Formula Assembly (Mixing Building Blocks)

The pre-work to form your building blocks will happen elsewhere (see the video-creative-engineering repository). Come to the assembly step armed with ideas.

High-performing concepts are generated by pairing each modular concept, using the 3-part framework, and constructing a seamless story from the sum of your parts.

Keep the narrative architecture stable, but don't plug-and-play without crafting a story that makes sense:

$$\text{Video Concept} = \text{Hook Variant [A]} + \text{Body Style [B]} + \text{Resolution [C]}$$

